   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Qa0yO5Al9UYn"
   },
   "source": [
    "**Note**:\n",
    "- After running the above cell, kindly restart the runtime (for Google Colab) or notebook kernel (for VSCode/Jupyter Notebook), and run all cells sequentially from the next cell.\n",
    "- On executing the above line of code, you might see a warning regarding package dependencies. This error message can be ignored as the above code ensures that all necessary libraries and their dependencies are maintained to successfully execute the code in ***this notebook***."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "qJFjRuvv9UYn"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Standard Library \n",
    "import json \n",
    "import os \n",
    "import re\n",
    "import sqlite3\n",
    "\n",
    "# Data and Numeric\n",
    "import numpy as np \n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import sqlparse\n",
    "\n",
    "# LLM and Schema\n",
    "from langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI\n",
    "from IPython.display import display"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "maq2rbmc9UYo"
   },
   "source": [
    "## **Data Loading and Model Initialization**\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "JBSkh3Vw_FXe"
   },
   "source": [
    "### OpenAI API Calling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "emfyg_ztFUEN"
   },
   "source": [
    "We load OpenAI credentials from a secure config.json file and store them as environment variables.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "NUkYwfvL9UYp"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the JSON file and extract values\n",
    "file_name = 'config.json'                                                       # Name of the configuration file\n",
    "with open(file_name, 'r') as file:                                              # Open the config file in read mode\n",
    "    config = json.load(file)                                                    # Load the JSON content as a dictionary\n",
    "    OPENAI_API_KEY = config.get('OPENAI_API_KEY')                               # Extract the API key from the config\n",
    "    OPENAI_API_BASE = config.get('OPENAI_API_BASE')                             # Extract the OpenAI base URL from the config\n",
    "\n",
    "# Store API credentials in environment variables\n",
    "os.environ['OPENAI_API_KEY'] = OPENAI_API_KEY                                   # Set API key as environment variable\n",
    "os.environ['OPENAI_BASE_URL'] = OPENAI_API_BASE                                 # Set API base URL as environment variable"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ltwfVxGM9UYq",
    "scrolled": true
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "llm: Okay\n",
      "evaluator_llm: Okay\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Generation LLM: handles intent classification, SQL generation, retry, and response writing\n",
    "# Temperature 0 keeps SQL and routing decisions deerministic and reproducible\n",
    "llm = ChatOpenAI(model = 'gpt-4o-mini', temperature = 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Evaluator LLM: a different model used only in validate_query's relevance check \n",
    "# Using separate, stronger model avoids the generator grading its own work \n",
    "evaluator_llm = ChatOpenAI(model = 'gpt-4o', temperature = 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quick check to esnure tha both models respond\n",
    "print('llm:', llm.invoke('Reply with the word Okay').content) \n",
    "print('evaluator_llm:', evaluator_llm.invoke('Reply with the word Okay').content)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "LLM choice rationale: gpt-4o-mini is used for generation because the tasks (routing, SQL writing, short summaries) are well-structured, and it is fast and low-cost which supports the under 2 minute and under 5 minute turnaround targetts. gpt-4o is used as the evaluator because relevance checking needs stronger reasoning, and using a different model from the generator prevents it from simply approving its own output. Temperature is 0 for both so results are reproducible and audible. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "NwkIY0Ru9UYq"
   },
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "### Database Loading"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "PIowRkuzFuBs"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Database connection established (read only mode)\n",
      "Tables found: ['sector_master', 'loan_master', 'borrower_rating', 'provisioning']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Path to the database file \n",
    "db_path = 'credit_risk_portfolio.db'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Read only connection: mode = ro makes SQLite reject any write operation\n",
    "conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{db_path}?mode=ro', uri = True)\n",
    "print('Database connection established (read only mode)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify all 4 tables are accessible \n",
    "tables = pd.read_sql_query(\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = 'table' AND name NOT LIKE 'sqlite_%'\", conn)\n",
    "print('Tables found:', tables['name'].tolist())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "WbNGXZbS9UYr"
   },
   "source": [
    "**Connect to the SQLite Database**\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a **read-only connection** to the provided SQLite database using `sqlite3`. Use URI mode with `?mode=ro` to prevent any write operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Sample code:**\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "import sqlite3\n",
    "\n",
    "conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{db_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Database connection established (read-only mode)\")\n",
    "```\n"
   ]
  },
