  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "xCbcVP7N9UYu"
   },
   "source": [
    "## **Verified Query Template Library**\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "AbQnMgPx_gOv"
   },
   "source": [
    "The Verified Query Template Library contains ten pre-approved SQL queries covering the most common recurring questions in credit risk analytics. Each template returns a complete result set, and the LLM writes a focused narrative from the full result based on what the user actually asked.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each entry has a unique identifier, a plain-English description used for intent matching, and a fixed SQL statement that runs without modification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "bfuUMkrjI7qI"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "fVPzjb4yI_Cf"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ1: Sector-wise Outstanding and NPA Breakdown\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate the total outstanding exposure and NPA exposure for each sector.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use `loan_master` for loan and outstanding information.\n",
    "2. Join `sector_master` using `sector_code` to get the sector name.\n",
    "3. Calculate total `total_outstanding` for each sector.\n",
    "4. Calculate NPA exposure using `asset_classification` values `Substandard`, `Doubtful`, and `Loss`.\n",
    "5. Convert both amounts to millions.\n",
    "6. Group the results by sector.\n",
    "7. Sort by total outstanding exposure in descending order.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "bW2RavvSI_L0"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_1 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT\n",
    "    s.sector_name,\n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(l.total_outstanding)/1e6, 2) AS total_outstanding_mn,\n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(CASE WHEN l.asset_classification IN ('Substandard', 'Doubtful', 'Loss') \n",
    "        THEN l.total_outstanding ELSE 0 END)/1e6, 2) AS npa_outstanding_mn\n",
    "FROM loan_master l\n",
    "JOIN sector_master s ON l.sector_code = s.sector_code\n",
    "GROUP BY s.sector_name\n",
    "ORDER BY total_outstanding_mn DESC\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "nTgvDV1UJTu5"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "0FzmWDP1JTu5"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ2: Portfolio Outstanding by Loan Category\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate the total outstanding exposure and loan count for each loan category.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `loan_master` table.\n",
    "2. Group the loans by `loan_category`.\n",
    "3. Calculate the sum of `total_outstanding` for each category.\n",
    "4. Count the number of loans in each category.\n",
    "5. Convert outstanding exposure to millions.\n",
    "6. Sort the results by outstanding exposure in descending order.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Zp5OGX9LJTu5"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_2 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    loan_category,\n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(total_outstanding) / 1e6, 2) AS total_outstanding_mn,\n",
    "    COUNT(*) AS loan_count\n",
    "FROM loan_master\n",
    "GROUP BY loan_category\n",
    "ORDER BY total_outstanding_mn DESC\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "YeUZ79BZJaTr"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "i4QDMPGBJaTr"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ3: IFRS 9 Stage-wise ECL Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Summarize loan exposure and expected credit loss by IFRS 9 stage for the latest reporting quarter.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `provisioning` table.\n",
    "2. Filter records for `reporting_date = '2025-09-30'`.\n",
    "3. Group the results by `ifrs9_stage`.\n",
    "4. Count the number of loans in each stage.\n",
    "5. Calculate total `ead_amount` and `ecl_amount` for each stage.\n",
    "6. Convert EAD and ECL to millions.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "wKc-UTO-JaTs"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_3 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT\n",
    "    ifrs9_stage,\n",
    "    COUNT(*) AS loan_count,\n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(ead_amount)/1e6, 2) AS total_ead_mn,\n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(ecl_amount)/1e6, 2) AS total_ecl_mn\n",
    "FROM provisioning\n",
    "WHERE reporting_date = '2025-09-30'\n",
    "GROUP BY ifrs9_stage\n",
    "ORDER BY ifrs9_stage\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Fj88EvMJJgTo"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "q4_1Gek1JgTo"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ4: Provision Coverage Ratio by Sector\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate the average Provision Coverage Ratio for each sector for the latest reporting quarter.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use `provisioning` for provision coverage information.\n",
    "2. Join `loan_master` using `loan_account_number`.\n",
    "3. Join `sector_master` using `sector_code`.\n",
    "4. Filter for `reporting_date = '2025-09-30'`.\n",
    "5. Calculate the average `provision_coverage_ratio` for each sector.\n",
    "6. Group the results by sector.\n",
    "7. Sort by average coverage ratio in descending order.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "1hvHgg1hJgTo"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_4 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    s.sector_name,\n",
    "    ROUND(AVG(p.provision_coverage_ratio), 2) AS avg_provision_coverage_ratio\n",
    "FROM provisioning p\n",
    "JOIN loan_master l ON p.loan_account_number = l.loan_account_number\n",
    "JOIN sector_master s ON l.sector_code = s.sector_code\n",
    "WHERE p.reporting_date = '2025-09-30'\n",
    "GROUP BY s.sector_name\n",
    "ORDER BY avg_provision_coverage_ratio DESC\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "QxtRhVEVJmIx"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ky44fn8ZJmIy"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ5: Top 10 Loan Exposures\n",
    "\n",
    "Identify the 10 individual loans with the highest outstanding exposure.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `loan_master` table.\n",
    "2. Select the borrower name, sector, outstanding amount, and asset classification.\n",
    "3. Use `total_outstanding` to represent the loan exposure.\n",
    "4. Convert outstanding exposure to millions.\n",
    "5. Sort loans by outstanding exposure in descending order.\n",
    "6. Return only the top 10 loans.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "EqyuYkB9JmIy"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_5 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT\n",
    "    l.borrower_name,\n",
    "    s.sector_name,\n",
    "    ROUND(l.total_outstanding/1e6, 2) AS total_outstanding_mn,\n",
    "    l.asset_classification\n",
    "FROM loan_master l\n",
    "JOIN sector_master s ON l.sector_code = s.sector_code\n",
    "ORDER BY l.total_outstanding DESC\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ETNW-5uoJt2a"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "jCLiliK1Jt2b"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ6: Top 5 Business Group Exposures\n",
    "\n",
    "Identify the five business groups with the highest total outstanding exposure.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `loan_master` table.\n",
    "2. Exclude records where `group_name` is missing.\n",
    "3. Group the loans by `group_name`.\n",
    "4. Count the loans within each group.\n",
    "5. Calculate total `total_outstanding` for each group.\n",
    "6. Convert exposure to millions.\n",
    "7. Sort groups by total exposure in descending order.\n",
    "8. Return only the top five groups.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "lWK-XEc2Jt2b"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_6 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    group_name, \n",
    "    COUNT(*) AS loan_count, \n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(total_outstanding)/1e6, 2) AS total_outstanding_mn\n",
    "FROM loan_master\n",
    "WHERE group_name IS NOT NULL \n",
    "GROUP BY group_name\n",
    "ORDER BY total_outstanding_mn DESC\n",
    "LIMIT 5\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "qKcMplfOJ2OQ"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "xztBEBrcJ2OR"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ7: All Overdue Loan Accounts\n",
    "\n",
    "Identify all loans that are currently overdue and show their delinquency information.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `loan_master` table.\n",
    "2. Filter for loans where `days_past_due > 0`.\n",
    "3. Return the loan account number, borrower name, sector, outstanding amount, DPD, and asset classification.\n",
    "4. Convert outstanding exposure to millions.\n",
    "5. Sort the results by `days_past_due` in descending order.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "BhjglCXsJ2OR"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_7 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    l.loan_account_number,\n",
    "    l.borrower_name,\n",
    "    s.sector_name,\n",
    "    ROUND(l.total_outstanding/1e6, 2) AS total_outstanding_mn,\n",
    "    l.days_past_due,\n",
    "    l.asset_classification\n",
    "FROM loan_master l \n",
    "JOIN sector_master s ON l.sector_code = s.sector_code\n",
    "WHERE l.days_past_due > 0\n",
    "ORDER BY l.days_past_due DESC\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "KgNwWKhiJ9V9"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "pSzDa1uTJ9V9"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ8: DPD Bucket Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "Show how loans and outstanding exposure are distributed across different Days Past Due buckets.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `loan_master` table.\n",
    "2. Create the following buckets based on `days_past_due`:\n",
    "\n",
    "   * `0 (Current)` for 0 days\n",
    "   * `1-30` for 1 to 30 days\n",
    "   * `31-60` for 31 to 60 days\n",
    "   * `61-90` for 61 to 90 days\n",
    "   * `90+` for more than 90 days\n",
    "3. Count the loans in each bucket.\n",
    "4. Calculate total outstanding exposure for each bucket.\n",
    "5. Convert exposure to millions.\n",
    "6. Order the buckets from current to highest DPD.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "iUzUvAoZJ9V9"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_8 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    CASE\n",
    "        WHEN days_past_due = 0 THEN '0 (Current)'\n",
    "        WHEN days_past_due BETWEEN 1 AND 30 THEN '1-30'\n",
    "        WHEN days_past_due BETWEEN 31 AND 60 THEN '31-60'\n",
    "        WHEN days_past_due BETWEEN 61 AND 90 THEN '61-90'\n",
    "        ELSE '90+'\n",
    "    END AS dpd_bucket, \n",
    "    COUNT(*) AS loan_count, \n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(total_outstanding)/1e6, 2) AS total_outstanding_mn\n",
    "FROM loan_master\n",
    "GROUP BY dpd_bucket\n",
    "ORDER BY MIN(days_past_due)\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "FgCjvKwOKDk4"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "K3fClJ83KDk4"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ9: Latest Rating Downgrades\n",
    "\n",
    "Identify borrowers whose internal credit rating was downgraded in the latest rating cycle.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `borrower_rating` table.\n",
    "2. Filter for `rating_date = '2025-09-30'`.\n",
    "3. Filter for `rating_direction = 'Downgraded'`.\n",
    "4. Return borrower ID, previous rating, current internal rating, and PD estimate.\n",
    "5. Sort the results by `pd_estimate` in descending order.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "B_A6VNgsKDk4"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_9 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    borrower_id,\n",
    "    previous_rating, \n",
    "    internal_rating AS current_rating,\n",
    "    pd_estimate\n",
    "FROM borrower_rating\n",
    "WHERE rating_date = '2025-09-30' AND rating_direction = 'Downgraded'\n",
    "ORDER BY pd_estimate DESC\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "M1W2rIqAKMwB"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query 10"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "1Q9Ynl5KKJaR"
   },
   "source": [
    "VQ10: ECL Trend Across Reporting Quarters\n",
    "\n",
    "Show how total Expected Credit Loss has changed across reporting quarters.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Steps:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Use the `provisioning` table.\n",
    "2. Group the records by `reporting_date`.\n",
    "3. Calculate the total `ecl_amount` for each reporting date.\n",
    "4. Convert ECL to millions.\n",
    "5. Sort the results chronologically by reporting date.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "wZAKBb8pKK2j"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sql_10 = \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT \n",
    "    reporting_date,\n",
    "    ROUND(SUM(ecl_amount)/1e6, 2) AS total_ecl_mn\n",
    "FROM provisioning\n",
    "GROUP BY reporting_date\n",
    "ORDER BY reporting_date\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "wzILnOUvKPaK"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verified Query Library"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "QmvPVFv6PWyk"
   },
   "source": [
    "The below code creates a dictionary-based **Verified Query Library**, where each query ID (`VQ1`, `VQ2`, etc.) is mapped to its description and corresponding SQL query.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Ih9pcsUo9UYu"
   },
   "outputs": [
