   "source": [
    "**Observation:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- The generated track correctly recognized that no template covers a Stage 3 trend, produced valid SQL, passed validation with 0.95 confidence, and returned all four quarters in date order with the expected Stage 3 EAD (from \\\\$346.25 million to \\\\$1,208.23 million) and ECL (from \\\\$131.73 million to \\\\$512.40 million).\n",
    "- An earlier run was escalated because the validator, which does not see the schema, assumed a date filter was needed, and a later run used outstanding balances instead of EAD. Giving the validator context about the four quarterly snapshots and instructing the generator to use ead_amount for stage and trend questions fixed both. The narrative describes the escalation in both exposure and ECL without computing any figures itself, although it mentions only the first and last quarters. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "tn4GdMrB9UY5"
   },
   "source": [
    "## **Evaluation Against Ground Truth**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Z0ICyTUUvg2T"
   },
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "Each test case output is compared against the corresponding ground-truth values to verify whether the correct route and query template were selected and whether the numeric answer aligns with expectations. This evaluation:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Calculates **Selected Path Accuracy**, **Selected Query Accuracy**, and **Average Confidence Score**.\n",
    "* Summarizes each test case with its route, query ID, confidence score, and rows returned.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "8lyato3I8Es9"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Selected Path Accuracy: 100.0%\n",
      "Selected Query Accuracy: 100.0%\n",
      "Average Confidence Score: 0.91\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "evaluation_rows = []\n",
    "\n",
    "test_results = [test_1, test_2, test_3, test_4, test_5]\n",
    "\n",
    "for i, (_, gt) in enumerate(ground_truth.iterrows()):\n",
    "    tr = test_results[i]\n",
    "\n",
    "    evaluation_rows.append({\n",
    "        'Test Case': gt['Test Case'],\n",
    "        'Expected Route': gt['Expected Route'],\n",
    "        'Actual Route': tr['route'],\n",
    "        'Route Match': tr['route'] == gt['Expected Route'],\n",
    "        'Expected Query ID': gt['Expected Query ID'],\n",
    "        'Actual Query ID': tr['query_id'],\n",
    "        'Query ID Match': (\n",
    "            pd.isna(gt['Expected Query ID']) and pd.isna(tr['query_id'])\n",
    "        ) or tr['query_id'] == gt['Expected Query ID'],\n",
    "        'Confidence': tr['confidence'],\n",
    "        'Rows Returned': tr['row_count']\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "evaluation_df = pd.DataFrame(evaluation_rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "path_accuracy = evaluation_df['Route Match'].mean() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "verified = evaluation_df['Expected Route'].str.strip().str.lower() == 'verified'\n",
    "query_accuracy = evaluation_df.loc[verified, 'Query ID Match'].mean() * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "average_confidence = evaluation_df['Confidence'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Selected Path Accuracy: {path_accuracy:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Selected Query Accuracy: {query_accuracy:.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"Average Confidence Score: {average_confidence:.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "nqQWO4WITUGI"
   },
   "source": [
    "**Observation:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Path accuracy and query accuracy were both 100%, with an average confidence of 0.91, so the engine routed all five questions to the correct track and template.\n",
    "- These metrics measure routing only, not whether the numbers are right. Confidence stayed at 0.9 or above even in earlier runs where the SQL or narrative was wrong, so the gate's score can't be trusted as a correctness signal.\n",
    "- Numeric accuracy was checked manually against the database: Real Estate outstanding \\\\$1,195.12 and NPA \\\\$89.93 (Test 1); 49 loans in the 90+ DPD bucket (Test 2); 35 restructured loans with 24 impaired, or 68.57% (Test 3); Pharmaceuticals highest average rate at 11.16% (Test 4); and Stage 3 EAD rising from \\\\$346.25 to \\\\$1,208.23 (Test 5). "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
